  "body": "Closes #1180\nClaim: cloud/fb-quickwins-sonnet\nAuthor model: Sonnet 5.5 (cloud/fb-quickwins-sonnet)\nReviewer model: Opus 5.5 (cloud/r1265-opus)\n\n**Problem.** The composer's clipboard question (« Utiliser le presse-papiers ? ») was an alert answering « Non » / « Oui », and its cancel-role button (« Non », « Sans le presse-papiers ») still inserted the tag, so Esc / ⌘. on a hardware keyboard inserted it too: no button backed out of the tap.\n\n**Cause.** A port of legacy (`AnswerView.swift:530-557` @ 87fe0d1c): same alert, titles and roles. A deliberate difference (HIG: choices in a dialog, verb titles, « Annuler » titles the button that cancels).\n\n**Change.** A `confirmationDialog` whose buttons come from `Pending.choices` (`ComposerClipboardChoice.swift`): the answers (« Coller le lien », « Insérer [url=XXX] », « Insérer [url]XXX[/url] », « Insérer »), « Insérer sans le presse-papiers » (the plain tags, legacy's « Non »), and a last « Annuler » (`role: .cancel`) that only dismisses the question (`dismissPending`). `choose(_:for:)` applies a choice to the question it was shown for (the dialog clears `pending` before the action runs, LOT-087). Roles of the other composer dialogs are untouched. Overlap: draft #1223 also edits `ReplyComposerView.swift` (card growth), `@@ -148`, a different region. The dialog is attached to the whole composer like the close dialog next to it, so on iPad it is a popover on the composer, not on the tapped button: listed for the device check on #893.\n\n**Tests.** `ComposerClipboardChoiceTests`: every question ends with exactly one « Annuler »; no title is a plain Oui/Non; each question's titles; cancelling leaves the text unchanged (the test that shows the change: the old cancel button went to `declinePending` and inserted the tag); the clipboardless choice inserts `[url]mot[/url]`; the first choice uses the clipboard; each link form by its title inserts its own tags (`[url=XXX][/url]` vs `[url]XXX[/url]`); an accepted formatting question wraps the clipboard in the tag. The first run of the file was a compile failure (no `Pending.choices`), not a test failing for the right reason.\n\n### Ledger\n\n```changelog\n| UX | La question « Utiliser le presse-papiers ? » du composer propose des boutons nommés (Coller le lien, Insérer…) et un vrai « Annuler » qui n'insère rien, au lieu de Non / Oui dont le bouton d'annulation insérait la balise. | #1180 | `AnswerView.swift:530-557` @ `87fe0d1c` |\n```\n\n```gap-edit\nGAP-085\nSwiftHFR final: Formatting toolbar and insertion engine; the bar sits behind Aa at the end of the control row, hidden when the composer opens (legacy at 87fe0d1c, #653); the clipboard question has verb buttons and a real « Annuler » that inserts nothing (#1180).\n```\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CDvQG8jqNrseTphdnF",
