   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, cloud/r1265-opus-r2, round 2): APPROVE** — head 6ae517e0\n\nNo findings. Round-1 status:\n1. Fixed. `eachLinkFormInsertsItsOwnTags` and `insertingTheClipboardWrapsItInTheTag` now run `choose` on a `.linkChoice` and on an accepted `.formatting`. Traced with text \"ab\", range (1,0), clipboard \"https://example.org/\":\n   - `textCandidate` keeps the text without trimming it, so the question is `.linkChoice`.\n   - `.acceptAttribute` goes through `insertURLAttributeTags` and gives `a[url=https://example.org/][/url]b`.\n   - `.accept` goes through `acceptPending`, then `acceptLinkChoice(attribute:false)`, then `apply(.bbCode(.url))`, then `wrapWithBBCode`, and gives `a[url]https://example.org/[/url]b`.\n   - On \"x\" with range (1,0) and clipboard \"extrait\", `.bbCode(.quote)` makes a `.formatting` question; « Insérer » (exact title match, so not « Insérer sans… ») gives `x[quote]extrait[/quote]`.\n   - Mutants: `attribute:false` for `.acceptAttribute` gives the `[url]…[/url]` form, so the first expectation fails. Swapped kinds make both link expectations fail. Routing `.accept` to `declinePending` fails the quote test and `theFirstChoiceUsesTheClipboard`.\n2. Fixed. No old wording is left in the LOT-085 or LOT-174 specs or in `ComposerFormattingModel.swift`. The remaining « Oui »/« Non » strings in `App/` (`ReaderEditFlow`, `ReaderAlertFlow`, `MPStorageCreationChoice`, polls) belong to other dialogs and are out of scope.\n3. Fixed. The PR body names the iPad popover anchoring for the device check on #893.\n4. Fixed. The PR body now says the first run of the test file was a compile failure, not a test failing for the right reason.\n\nAlso checked:\n- `askingClipboard`'s setter calls `dismissPending` when the dialog closes before the action runs. `choose` acts on the question it is given (`current`), not on `pending`, so the action still applies.\n- Legacy roles match the PR's claim: `AnswerView.swift:530-557` @ 87fe0d1c gives the cancel role to the buttons that insert the tag.\n\n**Verified**\n- `git diff f94f35bf 6ae517e0` and the whole diff against `origin/dev-swift`.\n- Traced `tap`, `acceptPending`, `acceptLinkChoice`, `declinePending`, `apply`, `clamped`, `wrapWithBBCode`, `wrapSelectionWithURL`, `insertURLAttributeTags`, `textCandidate`, `urlCandidate` and `ComposerFixture.model` at 6ae517e0.\n- `swiftlint lint --strict` on `App/SwiftHFR/Composer` and the new test file: exit 0.\n- Searched for leftover mentions of the old buttons.\n- `ledger.py check-body --pr 1265`: 2 blocks ok. The `gap-edit` keeps the existing GAP-085 \"SwiftHFR final\" cell and adds to it.\n- Not run: build and tests.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
